 "result_text": "The mixed-up call order is fixed, and `A down` now prints before `L up`.\n\nTests that don't use layers go into the top-level suite. That suite only tears down the last class's `tearDownClass` when it finishes, which was after the layer suites had already run. So that `tearDownClass` ran in the middle of your such-tests, or even after their setup.\n\nThe fix is in `nose2/suite.py`. `LayerSuite.run` now tears down any pending class fixtures before it starts the layer's setup.\n\nI checked it with a small script: a plain `TestCase` with `setUpClass`/`tearDownClass` next to a `such` test with `has_setup`. Before the fix, the `such` setup came before the `TestCase`'s `tearDownClass`.\n\nNine unit tests and one functional test fail. The same nine unit failures and one functional failure appear with my change stashed, so they are pre-existing. I added no tests.",
